Skills
------
- OpenScience/runtime/skills/curated-scientific/ derives from K-Dense's
  scientific-agent-skills (MIT; LICENSE.scientific-agent-skills.md). Per-skill
  provenance is recorded in its inventory.json.
- OpenScience/capabilities/knowledge-compile/SKILL.md (and its copy under capability-skills/) adapts the page
  types, the read-before-write rule, synonym merging and the handling of disagreements of the llm-wiki skill of
  volcengine/OpenViking (examples/compile/ov-compile-skills/llm-wiki, Apache-2.0). The quotation protocol and the
  checks are EviMed's.
- OpenScience/runtime/skills/community/ and core/humanizer, core/humanizer-zh
  are third-party skills under the MIT License, each with its LICENSE file; the
  community skills' pinned sources are recorded in community/sources.json.

Contracts and notices of upstream services
-------------------------------------------
- OpenScience/packages/contracts/openmed/ keeps OpenMed's Apache-2.0 LICENSE and
  NOTICE (LICENSE.upstream, NOTICE.upstream). Reference contracts only; no
  OpenMed code or weights are included.
- OpenScience/deploy/tooluniverse/NOTICE: ToolUniverse (Apache-2.0), installed
  when its image is built, not included here.

Installed at image build time, not part of this repository
-----------------------------------------------------------
The runtime image installs, from archives pinned by digest in
OpenScience/deps-version.json: the DeepSeek Harness packages (@deepseek-ai/*),
the community DSH bundles dsh-cite, @changfenhuang/dsh-annotation and
dsh-mermaid, and LoopX (the loopx CLI and dsh-loopx-plugin, Apache-2.0). Their
licenses travel with those packages.

Data
----
- OpenScience/evals/statistical-analysis/fixtures/: see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt
  there (CC BY 4.0 data, BSD-3-Clause adapted reference code, LGPL-2 data from
  the R survival package, with the license text).
- 项目代码/vcr-engine/tests/fixtures/: data from the CRAN packages
  EmpiricalCalibration and maicplus, Apache-2.0, with their notices.
- OpenScience/runtime/mcp/evimed-research/test/fixtures/vcr_imports/: synthetic
  patient data (CC0 / Apache-2.0); license and digest per file in
  provenance.json.
- OpenScience/evals/title-to-paper/corpus-v3/fulltext/: open-access articles
  from Europe PMC under the license recorded per article in manifest.json,
  including CC BY-NC and CC BY-ND terms. Those articles are redistributed
  unmodified under their own licenses, which the MIT License does not override.
- 项目代码/knowledge-plugin/tests/fixtures/: captured public web pages and feeds,
  kept only to test parsing; their content belongs to the publishers.
